---
import Layout from '../../components/layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Angiogenesis Surface Area"
  description="A lung angiogenesis image-analysis method for segmenting phase-contrast tube networks and measuring projected surface area."
  currentPath="/research"
>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lung-image-analysis-method.css" />
  <div class="page-content method-page">
    <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/research/lung-image-analysis">&larr; Lung Image Analysis</a></nav>

    <section class="hero-panel network-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method summary</p>
      <h1>Angiogenesis surface area</h1>
      <p>A transparent segmentation workflow for phase-contrast tube-formation assays.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Purpose</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        The pipeline measures projected network area: pixels occupied by the dark angiogenic network.
        The primary output is area as a fraction of the usable field. Whole-frame values are retained as a comparator.
      </p>
      <figure class="summary-figure">
        <img src="/images/lung-image-analysis/angiogenesis-method.svg" alt="Schematic angiogenesis surface-area workflow" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Workflow</h2>
      <div class="method-card">
        <div class="step"><div class="badge">1</div><div><h3>Load images</h3><p>Read grayscale assay images. Use the parent folder as the condition label.</p></div><div class="diagram network"><span class="tube a"></span><span class="tube b"></span><span class="tube c"></span></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="badge">2</div><div><h3>Correct background</h3><p>Estimate local illumination with a broad Gaussian blur. Subtract image intensity from background so dark tubes become positive signal.</p></div><div class="diagram network"><span class="signal a"></span><span class="signal b"></span><span class="signal c"></span></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="badge">3</div><div><h3>Segment network</h3><p>Threshold the corrected dark signal. Remove small objects and close small gaps.</p></div><div class="diagram network"><span class="mask"></span><span class="tube a"></span><span class="tube b"></span><span class="tube c"></span></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="badge">4</div><div><h3>Mark usable field</h3><p>Estimate an analyzable ROI to avoid strong glare, shadows, and edge artifacts.</p></div><div class="diagram network"><span class="roi"></span><span class="tube a"></span><span class="tube b"></span><span class="tube c"></span></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="badge">5</div><div><h3>Skeletonize</h3><p>Reduce the network mask to one-pixel centerlines. This prepares tube length, branch, and junction metrics.</p></div><div class="diagram network"><span class="skeleton a"></span><span class="skeleton b"></span><span class="skeleton c"></span></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="badge">6</div><div><h3>Measure</h3><p>Report <code>network_surface_area_px / analyzable_area_px</code>, plus whole-frame area and component geometry.</p></div><div class="diagram network"><span class="roi"></span><span class="signal a"></span><span class="signal b"></span><span class="signal c"></span></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Outputs</h2>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Output</th><th>Role</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>surface_area_image_metrics.csv</code></td><td>Per-image area, ROI, skeleton, component, and threshold metrics.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>network_surface_area_fraction</code></td><td>Primary projected surface-area readout.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>component_measurements.csv</code></td><td>Connected-component geometry for segmented foreground objects.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>masks/</code>, <code>dark_signal/</code>, <code>overlays/</code></td><td>Local review artifacts. Not included on this public page.</td></tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="note">This public page describes the method only. It does not show unpublished result plots, raw fields, or review overlays.</section>
  </div>
</Layout>
